# VPN-only public surface

The **only** service intentionally reachable from the public internet is **WireGuard UDP** (`vpn.<domain>` → OVH LB → NodePort). Everything else (HTTPS apps, GitLab UI, git SSH, registry, APIs) is **VPN-internal**.

## Do

- Keep OVH LB listeners limited to WireGuard UDP
- Reach `scm`, `auth`, `git-ssh`, registry, etc. via WireGuard + CoreDNS split-DNS (`~maze.trading`)
- Use `HostName git-ssh.<domain>` for Git over SSH (CoreDNS → `gitlab-gitlab-shell` ClusterIP)

## Do not

- Add public TCP/HTTP/HTTPS listeners for GitLab, ingress, or git SSH
- Publish NodePort/LoadBalancer Services for app traffic
- “Fix” git access by exposing `scm.<domain>:22` or gitlab-shell on the internet
- Point public DNS for app hostnames at the LB floating IP (except `vpn.<domain>`)

## Why

Minimum attack surface: unauthenticated internet can only attempt WireGuard handshake; all SCM and control-plane access requires a provisioned VPN peer.
